WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
Imagine three boxes, each
holding exactly one litre.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.770
One holds air.

3
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.210
One holds water.

4
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.510
One holds solid steel.

5
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.290
They take up exactly the same space.

6
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.570
Yet you could lift the
air with one finger,

7
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.970
and you'd feel the weight
of the steel straight away.

8
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.370
Same space, wildly
different amounts of stuff.

9
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.990
So why is the steel so much heavier?

10
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.970
In this mission, you'll meet density,

11
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.690
and calculate it from mass and volume.

12
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.950
You'll see how to measure the
mass and the volume of an object,

13
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.190
and use density to compare materials.

14
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.460
Your mission: explain why
the steel is so much heavier.
